> Does this mean, Death will instakill you, if you don't have MR?

Death's touch attack has the following damage properties:

If you're undead, simply does 8d8 damage. ("Was that the touch of death?")
Otherwise:
25%: nothing happens. ("Lucky for you, it didn't work!")
60%: does 8d8 damage, some or all of which may be applied to max HP
     as well as current ("You feel your life force draining away...")
15%: kills you outright unless you are magic resistant; if you are,
     does damage as in the above case.

(Rather misleadingly, the "sparkle" shield animation plays for the
"nothing happens" case iff you are magic resistant; this has nothing
to do with why nothing happened, which is a straight die-roll.)

